  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...Isolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms this \nafternoon and tonight. Isolated showers and thunderstorms possible \nMonday.\n\nA warm front will gradually lift north through the region through \nthis evening. Instability developing within the warm sector will aid \nscattered shower and thunderstorm development as a MCV currently \npushing east across the lower Ohio Valley impacts the region later \nthis afternoon. Severe thunderstorm potential looks limited with \nonly marginal instability and unfavorable shear profiles. PWATs \nrising to near 2.00\" will bring the potential for locally heavy \nrain, but this threat should remain isolated. The threat for \nadditional showers and embedded thunderstorms will continue tonight \nand Monday as a shortwave trough crosses the region later this \nevening, followed by a weak cold frontal passage late tonight and \nMonday.\n\nKey Message 2...A round of scattered showers and thunderstorms \nforecast for the midweek period.\n\nHigh pressure across the region Tuesday will exit by midweek, \nallowing a cold front to move through the region. Scattered showers \nand thunderstorms are expected late Tuesday night through Wednesday \nevening, with the best chances coming during the day Wednesday.",
